From: Modulo-Wifi maintainer
Subject: [PATCH] fix(enc28j60): avoid busy-spin and WDT starvation under RX pressure

When the DMA-capable heap is exhausted, heap_caps_malloc() for the RX buffer
returns NULL. The current code logs the error but stays in the do/while
(emac->packets_remain) loop, immediately retrying the allocation. Under
sustained pressure this becomes a tight busy-loop that can starve the task
watchdog and never yields to let lwIP free buffers.

On allocation failure, delay briefly and break out of the drain loop; the
interrupt re-triggers once buffers are available again. Also yield at the end
of each iteration during sustained packet floods, and NULL the buffer pointer
after ownership is transferred to the stack or after freeing, to make the
double-free protection explicit.

--- a/enc28j60/src/esp_eth_mac_enc28j60.c
+++ b/enc28j60/src/esp_eth_mac_enc28j60.c
@@ -- emac_enc28j60_task, "packet received" block
         // packet received
         if (status & EIR_PKTIF) {
             do {
                 length = ETH_MAX_PACKET_SIZE;
                 buffer = heap_caps_malloc(length, MALLOC_CAP_DMA);
                 if (!buffer) {
                     ESP_LOGE(TAG, "no mem for receive buffer");
+                    // Break out — don't spin. The interrupt will re-trigger
+                    // once lwIP frees buffers and we can allocate again.
+                    vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(5));
+                    break;
                 } else if (emac->parent.receive(&emac->parent, buffer, &length) == ESP_OK) {
                     /* pass the buffer to stack (e.g. TCP/IP layer) */
                     if (length) {
                         emac->eth->stack_input(emac->eth, buffer, length);
+                        buffer = NULL; // ownership transferred to stack
                     } else {
                         free(buffer);
+                        buffer = NULL;
                     }
                 } else {
                     free(buffer);
+                    buffer = NULL;
                 }
+                taskYIELD(); // prevent WDT starvation during sustained packet floods
             } while (emac->packets_remain);
         }
